    "text": "Privacy Policy Last updated November 8, 2018 Blog Freely , is built to enforce your right to privacy by default. It retains as little data about you as possible, not even requiring an email address to sign up. However, if you do give us your email address, it is stored encrypted in our database. We salt and hash your account's password. We store log files, or data about what happens on our servers. We also use cookies to keep you logged in to your account. Beyond this, it's important that you trust whoever runs Blog Freely . Software can only do so much to protect you \u2014 your level of privacy protections will ultimately fall on the humans that run this particular service.",
